KEY DESIGN FEATURES (v3.13)
---------------------------
- Single table format in Gold List and Highway
- One header per main set (not per sub-cluster)
- Clean artist names (no leading cluster prefixes)
- Consistent typography: 14pt section headers, 12pt data rows
- Date included in all document titles
- Version number (v3.13) clearly visible in all headers

DOCUMENT FORMATTING STANDARDS (v3.13)
-------------------------------------
Vertical Spacing:
  - All data rows use Pt(2) paragraph spacing before and after.

Centered Columns:
  - Alphabetic List: "Bit / Sample" column is centered (header + data)
  - Audio Hints: "Strategy" column is centered (header + data)
  - All other columns are left-aligned.

Current Column Widths (approximate):
  - Alphabetic List:     Artist-Album ~5.0",   Bit/Sample ~2.7"
  - Audio Hints:         Artist-Album ~2.57",  Strategy ~1.57",  Audio Hint ~3.57"
  - Golden List:         Artist ~2.2",         Album ~2.75",     Technical Phrase ~2.8"
  - Highway Subset:      Artist ~2.8",         Album ~3.2",      Technical Phrase ~4.0"

Header Styling:
  - Data table headers use dark blue background with bold text.
  - Set headers (Gold/Highway) use light gray background with bold 14pt text.
  - When a column is centered, its header cell is also centered.

DATA STRUCTURE
--------------
All nodes are stored in msl_data.py using a clean dictionary format:

    {
        "set_id": "07.4",
        "set_category": "Kinetic Action (Transient Speed)",
        "artist": "Makaya McCraven",
        "album": "In These Times",
        ...
    }

